---
import ResponsiveTable from './ResponsiveTable.astro';
import rSource from '../examples/code/financial-practice-trials.R?raw';
import presentation from '../data/financial-practice-trials.json';
---

<div class="trial-demo">
  <h3>Inspect a small fictional practice-trial analysis</h3>
  <p class="disclosure">
    Created independently for this portfolio using fictional data. It does not reproduce
    employer code, data, fields, rules, coefficients, model results, reports or system
    architecture. It demonstrates population preparation and association analysis, not a
    historical employer model or its performance.
  </p>
  <p>
    The intended unit is one observation per fictional practice trial. A separate group
    lookup must match each trial once. Completed means a recorded outcome of 1; 0 means
    not completed. A missing outcome excludes a trial from both summaries and modeling; a
    missing preparation measure excludes it only from modeling. Nothing is imputed.
  </p>
  <p>
    The descriptive comparison uses all trials with recorded outcomes. The model uses only
    trials with both outcome and preparation values. Practice group is context for the
    descriptive comparison, not a model predictor.
  </p>
  <p class="caption">
    On small screens, scroll the input table sideways to inspect every field.
  </p>
  <div class="trial-tables">
    {presentation.tables.map((table) => (
      <div id={table.id}>
        <ResponsiveTable label={table.caption + '; scroll horizontally if needed'}>
          <table
            class={
              table.id === 'trial-input'
                ? 'wide-table'
                : table.headers.length > 3
                  ? 'mobile-records'
                  : 'narrow-table'
            }
            role="table"
          >
            <caption>{table.caption}</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                {table.headers.map((header) => (
                  <th scope="col">{header}</th>
                ))}
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {table.rows.map((row) => (
                <tr>
                  {row.map((value, index) => (
                    <td data-label={table.headers[index]}>{value}</td>
                  ))}
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </ResponsiveTable>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="trial-boundary">
    <p>
      <strong>Interpret the association within its population.</strong> The synthetic odds
      ratio compares modeled completion odds for an additional preparation unit, assuming
      a linear relationship with log odds. It is not a change in probability. This tiny
      invented dataset is not evidence about real practice or group differences.
    </p>
    <p>
      An association in this fictional observational example does not establish causation
      or production predictive performance. Passing these checks does not prove that a
      model is universally valid. The example analyzes and reports results without
      modifying its source records. Its checks are not claims about checks performed in
      the historical professional studies.
    </p>
  </div>
  <details id="trial-code">
    <summary>Create, analyze and verify fictional trials · view base R source</summary>
    <p class="caption">
      Self-contained base R; no packages, database or network connection. Run the complete
      script to print the presentation tables as JSON. An optional output filename saves
      the same JSON for the static page. Negative fixtures must be rejected for the script
      to finish successfully.
    </p>
    <pre
      tabindex="0"
      aria-label="Complete fictional practice-trial R source"
    ><code>{rSource}</code></pre>
  </details>
</div>

<style>
  .trial-demo {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .disclosure {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--teal);
    padding-left: 14px;
  }
  .trial-tables {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    margin-block: 24px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .trial-tables > div {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .wide-table {
    min-width: 36rem;
  }
  .wide-table caption {
    max-width: 17rem;
  }
  .narrow-table {
    table-layout: fixed;
    width: 100%;
  }
  th,
  td {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .trial-boundary {
    padding: 18px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .trial-boundary p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  details {
    min-width: 0;
    margin-top: 24px;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  summary {
    padding: 14px 4px;
    min-height: 48px;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--teal);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  pre {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 32rem;
    overflow: auto;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
